1
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:13,500
Ascension is a documentary film directed by Jessica Kingdon.

2
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:21,000
The film explores the pursuit of the “Chinese Dream.” Driven by mesmerizing—and sometimes humorous—imagery, this observational
documentary presents a contemporary vision of China that prioritizes productivity and innovation above all.

3
00:36:22,500 --> 00:36:28,500
Ascension (Chinese: 登楼叹; pinyin: Dēnglóu tàn) is a 2021 American
documentary film directed and produced by Jessica Kingdon.

4
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
It follows the pursuit of the Chinese dream through the social
classes, prioritizing productivity and innovation.

5
01:00:37,500 --> 01:00:43,500
The film had its world premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival on
June 12, 2021, where it won Best Documentary Feature.

6
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:51,000
It was released on October 8, 2021, by MTV Documentary Films.

7
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:58,500
The film explores themes of factory worker, china,
working class, sex doll, economic inequality.
